      "prompt": "Use vendor/mako as a test target to test if fragilec can work as a drop-in compiler and pass all build and test. When you build, first make clean for clean build, then use -j32 for faster build.  You probably will see errors in output. Investigate the first error file and do a generic fix (don't do any mako-specific fixes or hacks in fragile). When you investigate this error, try build that file alone (with the proper include path  from cmake). Also remember to revise mako-dev-book in docs dir. Commit and push your fix. Then build the project again, find the next error file and repeat this process until you fix all error files. ",
