      "session_id": "3319cc66-19ee-4a9e-9d4d-ba11b943f69e",
      "is_paused": false,
      "stop_requested": false,
      "prompt": "Work in your own git worktree (codex/mako-safe-rust). Now we can compile vendor/mako using fragilec as a drop-in compiler and pass all build and test. Let us improve, many of mako's code is rusty-cpp safe. For these code, we should be able to transpile them into safe rust code. So improve your trasnpiler to try to transpile them into safe code and do test build and run tests. Rusty-cpp has a library for common rust-like types such as RefCell, HashMap, etc. Please transpile them to Rust std library. When you build, first make clean for clean build, then use -j32 for faster build.  You probably will see errors in output. Investigate the errors and try to do a generic fix (don't do any mako-specific fixes or hacks in fragile). If it is something that needs to fix rusty-cpp, you can also try to fix it in a generic way and push to its remote. If it is something that is worth documented, doc it into a section in fragile-dev-book in docs dir. Commit and push your fix. ",
